  "verbalization": "Luspatercept is associated with Beta-thalassemia And Related Diseases through a chain of indications involving Deferasirox. This relationship is supported by the shared use of Deferasirox as an indication for both Beta-thalassemia Intermedia and Beta-thalassemia Hbb/lcrb, which are subtypes of Beta-thalassemia. The presence of Deferasirox in these contexts suggests a potential mechanism of action or therapeutic relationship that links Luspatercept to the broader category of Beta-thalassemia. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible overlap in the clinical management of thalassemia, where Deferasirox is used to treat different subtypes, and Luspatercept may exert a similar effect in a broader context. The evidence underscores a potential mechanistic link that could be further explored to understand the role of Luspatercept in the treatment of thalassemia.",
